{
  "query": "# TASK-203: Dead-Letter Queue Routing for Malformed Schema Events in EventTransformer\n\n## Summary\nEvents arriving at the pipeline without a valid `event_id` currently raise an unhandled `SchemaError`, halting batch processing. Instead of terminating the pipeline, malformed events should be routed to the configured dead-letter queue.\n\n## Current Observed Behavior\n`EventTransformer.transform_event()` raises a `SchemaError` when `event_id` is missing.\n\n## Expected Behavior\nWhen an event is missing `event_id`, `EventTransformer` should route the invalid event and failure reason to `self.dead_letter.route(event, reason=\"Missing required event_id\")` and return `None` without raising an uncaught exception.\n",
